Subject: [PATCH] Add an aggregated setup rollup to the engagement page's
 Skills panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Answers this session's own question about how Stripe/Zapier surface
"what's left to configure" — both use a single rolled-up checklist
instead of making the user hunt card by card. Built directly on top of
the needs_setup work from the previous commit, same missing-fields
data, no new fetch.

The one hard requirement: never mislabel a plain on/off worker (20 of
34 — no required fields, nothing to ever configure) as an incomplete
setup step just because it happens to be enabled. The rollup's
denominator is built exclusively from the new CONFIG_CHECKED_WORKER_IDS
export (worker-config-completeness.ts's own CHECKERS keys — the same
14 workers this whole gating system has covered all session, nothing
newly invented), never from workerIds or enabledIds. Toggle-only
workers are named explicitly in a separate, clearly distinct line
("+3 other enabled skills are plain on/off — nothing to configure")
instead of being silently folded into either the numerator or the
denominator.

- worker-config-completeness.ts: exports CONFIG_CHECKED_WORKER_IDS,
  the one source of truth for "this worker has real required fields" —
  every future rollup should read this, not maintain its own list.
- workers-panel.tsx: new strip between the header and the card grid.
  Amber when something's incomplete, with each incomplete worker as a
  clickable chip (name + missing-field count) that jumps straight into
  its config form via the existing expandedWorker in-place swap — no
  new navigation pattern. Green "All N configured skills are fully set
  up" when nothing's left. Hidden entirely when no enabled worker in
  this list has any required fields at all (nothing to roll up).

Deliberately scoped to the engagement page only, where the missing-
fields data already lives — the Library page's own badge uses a
different, richer completeness signal (capability-matrix based, not
just blocking-tier fields) and wasn't touched here.

tsc clean (same 5 pre-existing unrelated test-file errors as baseline),
vitest unchanged at 59 failed/210 passed/18 skipped.

