From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: previous commit broke the client build (server-only
 import in a "use client" file)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Caught by next build, not tsc --noEmit — tsc alone missed this. The
rollup commit imported CONFIG_CHECKED_WORKER_IDS and MissingField
straight from worker-config-completeness.ts into workers-panel.tsx
("use client"). That file pulls in db (postgres) and credentials.ts
(which pulls in composio -> fs/os) — server-only dependencies that got
dragged into the client bundle, and Turbopack correctly refused to
build it ("Module not found: Can't resolve 'fs'").

Split the two client-safe pieces (the MissingField shape and the
CONFIG_CHECKED_WORKER_IDS list) into a new
worker-config-completeness-shared.ts with zero server imports.
worker-config-completeness.ts now imports from it instead of defining
its own copies, and re-exports MissingField for its existing server-side
consumers (src/app/dashboard/engagements/[id]/page.tsx). Workers-panel.tsx
now imports the shared file directly.

CONFIG_CHECKED_WORKER_IDS is necessarily a hand-written mirror of
CHECKERS' own keys now, not a derived value, since deriving it would
require importing the server file again. To keep the two from silently
drifting apart — which would recreate the exact mislabeling problem the
constant exists to prevent — worker-config-completeness.ts asserts at
module load (outside production) that its CHECKERS keys exactly match
the shared list, and throws if they don't.

Verified this time with the step that actually caught the bug: a real
`next build`, not just tsc --noEmit (which had stayed clean throughout —
tsc doesn't understand the client/server module boundary the way
Turbopack's bundler does). Compiles clean now, same pre-existing sandbox
DATABASE_URL limitation on page-data collection as every prior build
this session. tsc still clean at the same 5 pre-existing unrelated
test-file errors. vitest unchanged at 59 failed/210 passed/18 skipped.

